+## FFS-supervised-process compatibility mode
+
+FFS can provide an explicit process supervisor for recovery and for fixture
+repositories. This mode is selected only when the host sets
+`GSD_DISPATCH_MODE=ffs-supervised-process`; it is a process transport layered
+over the existing isolation decision, not a new `ISOLATION` value and never a
+reason to bypass the isolation guard. A host that has not demonstrated FFS
+admission must refuse the wave.
+
+Resolve the admission descriptor immediately before the first executor in the
+wave:
+
+```bash
+if [ "${GSD_DISPATCH_MODE:-}" = "ffs-supervised-process" ]; then
+  FFS_DISPATCH_JSON=$(gsd_run query dispatch-ffs-supervised --json --raw 2>/dev/null) || {
+    echo "FATAL: ffs-supervised-process was requested but FFS admission is unavailable; refusing to dispatch." >&2
+    exit 78
+  }
+  FFS_MODE=$(printf '%s' "$FFS_DISPATCH_JSON" | node -e 'let s="";process.stdin.on("data",d=>s+=d).on("end",()=>{try{let j=JSON.parse(s);process.stdout.write(j&&j.mode||"")}catch{}})')
+  [ "$FFS_MODE" = "ffs-supervised-process" ] || {
+    echo "FATAL: FFS admission did not return mode ffs-supervised-process; refusing to dispatch." >&2
+    exit 78
+  }
+fi
+```
