+   requesting any executor. Prepare every plan's complete, fresh prompt before
+   launching the first process. The FFS supervisor exclusively allocates and
+   registers each child worktree beneath the current run; GSD must not create
+   or name executor worktrees in this mode. Each manifest
+   plan carries `initial_head: "$EXPECTED_BASE"`, `prompt_fresh: true`, a
+   unique `prompt_nonce`, the SHA-256 of that exact prompt, `files_modified`,
+   `files_deleted`, and its original `depends_on` plan ids. Dependencies on
+   completed prior waves remain in the manifest for supervisor verification;
+   no plan may depend on another plan allocated in the same runnable wave.
+   A plan whose measured HEAD or prompt hash does not match is a fatal wave
